{number: 50}
{title: Have Thine Own Way, Lord}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own [Bb7] way!
Thou art the Potter,
I am the [Eb] clay.
Mould me and [Eb7] make me
After Thy [Ab] will,
While I am [Eb] waiting,
[Bb7] Yielded and [Eb] still.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own [Bb7] way!
Search me and try me,
Master, to-[Eb] day!
Whiter than [Eb7] snow, Lord,
Wash me just [Ab] now,
As in Thy [Eb] presence
[Bb7] Humbly I [Eb] bow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own [Bb7] way!
Wounded and weary,
Help me, I [Eb] pray.
Power, all [Eb7] power
Surely is [Ab] Thine!
Touch me and [Eb] heal me,
[Bb7] Savior di-[Eb] vine!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Eb] Have Thine own way, Lord!
Have Thine own [Bb7] way!
Hold o'er my being
Absolute [Eb] sway!
Fill with Thy [Eb7] Spirit
Till all shall [Ab] see
Christ only, [Eb] always,
[Bb7] Living in [Eb] me!
{end_of_verse}
